1. Toxtree (GPL-2.0) — (c) Ideaconsult Ltd. and contributors
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Several structural alerts in p62_toxicity_alerts.py derive from the
Benigni-Bossa rule base as implemented in Toxtree 3.1.0. Each is marked at its
point of definition; grep for "Attribution:" to list them all.

  verbatim from Toxtree 3.1.0 — the SMARTS string was transcribed unchanged
      mutant/rules/SA22_gen.java   azide / triazene alerts
      mutant/rules/SA1_gen.java    acyl halide alert
      mutant/rules/SA10_gen.java   alpha,beta-unsaturated carbonyls
                                   (present but currently disabled; see the
                                   note at its entry)

  adapted from Toxtree 3.1.0 — the pattern was narrowed or rewritten here
      mutant/rules/SA7_gen.java    epoxide / aziridine, narrowed to ring atoms
                                   with amide nitrogen excluded
      mutant/rules/SA12_gen.java   para- and ortho-quinone, bond primitives
                                   relaxed so aromatic-drawn quinones match

  independent reimplementation — decision logic only, no code or pattern copied
      mutant/rules SA18, SA19      carbocyclic and heterocyclic polycyclic
                                   aromatics, reimplemented with RDKit ring
                                   perception in _scan_pah()

No part of the Toxtree distribution is included in or redistributed with this
repository. Toxtree was run as a benchmark for the comparison reported in the
accompanying article, which is use rather than distribution.

