2. Ames mutagenicity dataset — no licence stated by the compiler
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Compiled by Therapeutics Data Commons (AMES, single-prediction toxicity),
hosted on Harvard Dataverse, doi:10.7910/DVN/21LKWG. The TDC toolkit is
MIT-licensed; the dataset itself carries no stated licence.

Neither the structures nor the labels are redistributed here. Only
data/ames_split_manifest.csv is included: InChIKeys, labels and the
train/validation assignment, which is sufficient to rebuild the exact splits
from the source dataset. See data/README.md.

Primary source cited by TDC:
  Xu, C.; Cheng, F.; Chen, L.; Du, Z.; Li, W.; Liu, G.; Lee, P.W.; Tang, Y.
  In Silico Prediction of Chemical Ames Mutagenicity.
  J. Chem. Inf. Model. 2012, 52, 2840-2847. doi:10.1021/ci300400a

The experimental record index also holds 29 records from the Hansen benchmark
(Hansen, K. et al. J. Chem. Inf. Model. 2009, 49, 2077-2081), 12 from Tox21 and
8 from ISSCAN.

